Reviewed the contract: standard admin setters are guarded by `governance`, `strategist`, or `timelock`; `withdraw` is guarded by `jars[_token]`; `yearn` and `inCase*` functions require strategist/governance; `earn` only transfers to the configured strategy and has no arbitrary recipient. The constructor is the actual constructor and is only callable at deployment.

The security-sensitive sink operations are the delegatecall primitive in `_execute` and the externally callable `swapExactJarForJar`, which invokes `_execute` with user-supplied calldata and performs token transfers using user-supplied jar addresses without validating them against the `jars` mapping.

